{"body":{"genre":"Sport","isPrivate":false,"text":"An internal admin tool is the easiest place to stop building a client data layer. One viewer, no SEO, no public traffic, and a question that is always ‘what is the state right now’. For the admin of my PDF-verification SaaS I built a React Server Components admin dashboard that fetches nothing from the browser: no query cache, no fetch hooks, no chart library. The title says ‘no client data layer’, not ‘zero JavaScript’. The admin tree has five Server Component pages. Mutations and a few interactive controls are small client components. What is missing is the layer that usually comes with a dashboard: a client-side cache, API routes that only exist to feed it, and loading states for every panel.","title":"Test"},"level":"info","message":"Incoming request","method":"GET","timestamp":"2026-11-08T15:57:43.993Z","url":"/api/newsposts/error"}
